{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "HDFC Bank Loan Portfolio—SMA Classification & Early Warning Logic",
  "scenario": "You are an analyst at a Mumbai research desk monitoring HDFC Bank's loan health. The RBI requires classification of accounts by days-past-due into buckets: Standard, SMA-0, SMA-1, SMA-2, and NPA. Your task is to build the classification logic, flag high-risk accounts, and compute key metrics using IF, AND, OR, IFS, and IFERROR.",
  "instructions": "Build classification formulas using nested IF and IFS logic; flag accounts meeting compound criteria (days overdue AND loan size); compute portfolio metrics with error-handling; validate results against three test rows (boundary cases).",
  "learning_objective": "Apply nested IF, IFS with catch-all, AND/OR compound conditions, and IFERROR to classify loan accounts into RBI-mandated SMA buckets, identify high-risk concentrations, and construct a self-checking portfolio dashboard.",
  "hints": [
    "RBI SMA buckets ascend strictly: 0 days → Standard, 1–30 → SMA-0, 31–60 → SMA-1, 61–90 → SMA-2, >90 → NPA. Write your nested IF so gates run in one direction only.",
    "For 'High Risk' (days > 60 AND size > ₹10 Cr), use AND inside the IF test. For 'Watch List' (days > 30 OR size > ₹50 Cr), use OR. Remember to multiply for AND scoring: =(B2>60)*(C2>10) equals 1 only when both hold.",
    "In the metrics row, P/E computation risks #DIV/0! when earnings are zero or missing. Wrap it in IFERROR(B2/C2, \"n/m\") to show 'n/m' for loss accounts. The tolerance check ABS(total_debit - total_credit) should be < 0.01."
  ],
